<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>How long do hearing aid firmware updates take?</h3>
<p>Plan on 5–30 minutes, depending on your brand, the size of the update, and your phone’s connection. Keep both aids charged and your phone awake with the app open. Some major updates can take longer—your app will typically warn you.</p>

<h3>Will a firmware update erase my custom programs or settings?</h3>
<p>Most updates keep your programs and gains intact. If a core algorithm changes, the sound may feel a bit different. If something seems off afterward, contact your audiologist for a quick fine-tune.</p>

<h3>Can a firmware update fix tinnitus?</h3>
<p>Updates won’t cure tinnitus. Occasionally they add or improve sound options that can help some people mask or manage tinnitus. If tinnitus is bothering you, talk with an audiologist about personalized strategies.</p>

<h3>Is it safe to update while my rechargeable aids are in the charger?</h3>
<p>Yes—many brands recommend updating on the charger for stable power. Follow your app’s instructions. Avoid removing the aids or turning off your phone mid-update.</p>


